---
/**
 * PDPA notice, a short standalone statement of Singapore Personal Data
 * Protection Act 2012 compliance, with pointers to the detail in
 * /privacy. Keeping this short and separate makes the PDPA-specific
 * obligations (DPO, consent, withdrawal, access & correction) findable in
 * one place, without duplicating the full privacy policy.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import client from '../config/client.ts';

const { company, legal, contact } = client;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="PDPA Notice"
  intro={`${company.legalName}'s statement of compliance with Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act 2012.`}
>
  <h2>1. Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName} (<strong>{company.registrationNumber}</strong>) is
    committed to protecting your personal data in accordance with the Singapore
    Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (the “PDPA”) and its subsidiary
    legislation, and the advisory guidelines issued by the Personal Data
    Protection Commission of Singapore (“PDPC”).
  </p>
  <p>
    This notice summarises how we comply with the PDPA. Our full
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}contains the operational detail, what we collect, how we use it, who we share it with and how long we keep
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Purposes for collecting your personal data</h2>
  <p>
    We collect, use and disclose personal data for purposes a reasonable person
    would consider appropriate in the circumstances, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Responding to your enquiries and preparing quotations</li>
    <li>Scheduling and carrying out painting and waterproofing work</li>
    <li>Contacting you about your project by phone, SMS, WhatsApp or email</li>
    <li>Providing customer support and warranty service</li>
    <li>Billing, accounting and tax record-keeping</li>
    <li>Sending you marketing information where you have consented</li>
    <li>Preventing fraud and misuse of our services</li>
    <li>Meeting legal, regulatory and contractual obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where we intend to use your personal data for a new purpose that is not
    covered above, we will notify you and obtain your consent before doing so
    (unless the PDPA permits or requires the use without further consent).
  </p>

  <h2>3. Consent</h2>
  <p>
    By submitting an enquiry, engaging our services, or otherwise providing
    personal data to us, you consent to us collecting, using and disclosing
    your personal data for the purposes described in Section 2 and in our full
    Privacy Policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where we ask for your consent to receive SMS or WhatsApp messages from us
    about your enquiry, that consent is a separate opt-in confirmed by ticking
    the consent box on our enquiry form. You may withdraw that consent at any
    time by replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Withdrawal of consent</h2>
  <p>
    You may withdraw your consent to our continued collection, use or
    disclosure of your personal data at any time by contacting our Data
    Protection Officer (Section 7).
  </p>
  <p>
    Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried
    out before withdrawal. Withdrawing consent may limit our ability to respond
    to your enquiry, complete work you have engaged us for, or provide warranty
    support, we will let you know the specific consequences at the time.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Access and correction</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right, under the PDPA, to request:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      confirmation of the personal data we hold about you and how it has been
      used or disclosed in the past year; and
    </li>
    <li>
      that we correct any errors or omissions in that personal data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Requests can be sent to our Data Protection Officer at the details in
    Section 7. We will respond within 30 days, or notify you of the time we
    require if we cannot meet that deadline. A reasonable fee may apply to
    access requests as permitted by the PDPA.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Protection, accuracy and retention</h2>
  <p>
    We apply reasonable security arrangements to protect personal data in our
    possession or under our control from unauthorised access, collection, use,
    disclosure, copying, modification, disposal or similar risks. We take
    reasonable steps to ensure the personal data we hold is accurate and
    complete. We retain personal data only for as long as it is needed for the
    purposes for which it was collected, or as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data Protection Officer</h2>
  <p>
    We have appointed a Data Protection Officer as required under Section 11(3)
    of the PDPA. All queries, requests and complaints relating to your personal
    data should be directed to:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Data Protection Officer</strong><br />
    {company.legalName}<br />
    {contact.address.line1}<br />
    {contact.address.city} {contact.address.postalCode}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.privacyEmail}`}>{legal.privacyEmail}</a><br />
    Telephone: <a href={`tel:${contact.phoneHref}`}>{contact.phone}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>8. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your personal data or
    your request, you may lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection
    Commission of Singapore at{' '}
    <a href="https://www.pdpc.gov.sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      www.pdpc.gov.sg
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-brand-muted">
    This notice was last updated on {legal.lastUpdated}. We may revise this
    notice from time to time; the current version is always available at this
    page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
